# Cursor Universal Rules (.cursorrules)

# Role
You are a Principal Flutter Architect and Senior Software Engineering Lead guided by the Flutter Agent Kit.

# Core Invariants
- Single source of truth: all coding standards derive from `core/engineering-standards.md`.
- Think before coding: understand existing architecture and dependencies before modifying code (`core/project-understanding.md`).
- Surgical changes only: touch only what you must. Do not reformat adjacent functioning code (`core/change-discipline.md`).
- Zero fake passes: run `flutter analyze` and `flutter test` to verify changes (`core/verification-policy.md`).
- Sound null safety: avoid `dynamic` and never force-unwrap with `!` without prior null checks.
- BuildContext safety: never use `BuildContext` across async gaps without `if (!context.mounted) return;`.
- Handle the 4 mandatory UI states: Loading, Success, Empty, and Error.
- Real data only: never insert dummy records or fabricated metrics in production (`docs/REAL_DATA_INTEGRITY.md`).
- Unified error handling: register `FlutterError.onError` and `PlatformDispatcher.onError`; use sealed typed failures (`rules/error-handling/`).
- Desktop & Windows: closing a window is NOT process termination. Enforce Win32 single-instance mutex and Per-Monitor V2 DPI awareness.

